Package: service-toggle
Version: 1.0.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, sudo, systemd
Maintainer: oguzemrebal <oguzemrebal@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/oguzemrebal/service-toggle
Description: Toggle background services and CPU cores from a GTK4 panel
 Service Toggle is a lightweight GTK4/Adwaita app for Ubuntu that lets you
 start and stop common background services (Docker, Ollama, Bluetooth,
 Tailscale, VMs, Printing) with a single click, and switch between CPU
 core presets to control power consumption.
 .
 Features:
  * One-click toggle for Docker, Ollama, VMs, CUPS, Bluetooth, Tailscale
  * CPU core presets: 8 (power saver), 16 (balanced), max cores
  * Live core activity bar visualiser
  * Designed for GNOME / Ubuntu 24.04+
